  "notes": "Cause code X ('Other') governs category per official coding despite narrative describing a maintenance/human-error-leaning causal investigation; theme captures the loose-connection angle. Both DG trains were inoperable at overlapping but not simultaneous times (2A DG inoperable briefly on 7/2 and 7/10; 2B DG failure discovered 7/15) — narrative states this combination is what makes the event reportable under 50.73(a)(2)(i)(B) and (a)(2)(v)(D) for both units, so cons_both_inop is modeled as a distinct downstream consequence from the initial 2B DG inoperability. ESPS, SSF DG, and FLEX are described as available defense-in-depth/recovery means (Safety Analysis section) rather than pure design-context narrative, so they are modeled as BACKED_UP_BY per rule 6; SATA/offsite power from Unit 1 was omitted as it was described conditionally ('if available') without confirmation of operability during this event."
